      "file": "forced_circulation_evaporator_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Hydrostatic head suppresses boiling in the tubes",
      "description": "The circulation pump drives liquid through the tubes at high velocity (typically ~ 1.5–3 m/s). The static head above the tubes keeps the liquid under enough pressure that it is only heated (a few °C) without boiling; it flashes when it reaches the separator. Suppressing boiling at the wall prevents scaling and crystal deposition — ideal for crystallising, scaling or viscous liquids.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
